Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:38:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sharpen the three new eval sets and close two coherence gaps

A value pass over the eval sets this branch authored, on gradeability rather
than correctness. Three expectations were conditionals on states the eval
never creates, so two judges would score the same transcript differently:
research's usage-threshold halt, health-check's stale-decision-record case,
and health-check's advisory case, whose expectations named the eval-coverage
and orphans advisories that no longer fire - eval-coverage precisely because
this branch authored the three missing sets. Each now grades what the
transcript actually shows.

Also splits a health-check expectation that asserted two things at once, and
replaces an unfalsifiable cursor-projection expectation ("does not answer
from memory") that duplicated the harness-matrix load check above it with the
readonly: claim its expected_output already promised but never graded.

Relabels three expectations from judgment to deterministic. Each is a binary
fact about the transcript - whether an Agent call occurred, which
subagent_type was passed, whether a sentence appears - and evals/README.md
grades deterministic checks at 100 percent against judgment's 90 percent
aggregate, so the label was scoring real misses leniently.

Rewraps README.md's reference/ inventory, which the model-selection.md entry
had turned into a run-on with the list and its parentheticals colliding.

Moves specs/behaviors.md's Config Health Check eval note to the end of the
section and states what now exists. It led the section, above Purpose, as the
repository's only such note and the only behaviors.md section not opening
with Registration, Decision, or Purpose - and it had gone stale, reading as
though no negative-trigger test existed when specs/skills.md records one
authored but unrun.
